### How to use this guide
- Don't memorize answers verbatim — internalize the structure (Situation → Action → Result) and practice saying them naturally.
- For the behavioral questions (Section 6), have 5–6 core stories ready that you can flex across multiple questions — most interviewers are really probing for the same 5–6 underlying signals.
- Update Q98 with your genuine, current motivation before any real interview.


